sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Agent code
    participant F as adapters.<framework>._Replay*
    participant W as wrapped framework model
    participant S as active_session()
    participant Sig as extract_signature
    participant Cursor as ReplaySession cursor
    participant C as _common.build_live_span
    participant DB as rewind.db

    Note over A,DB: Setup: trace seeded with N LLM spans.<br/>ReplaySession opened in BRANCH mode.<br/>Calls 0..N-1 match; call N will diverge.

    Note over A,DB: Stage 1 — first N-1 calls served from cache (identical to FROZEN)
    loop i ∈ [0, N)
        A->>F: generate_response(request_i)
        F->>S: active_session()
        F->>Sig: extract_signature(...)
        F->>Cursor: respond_or_forward(signature_i)
        Cursor-->>F: RecordedResponse(payload_i)
        F-->>A: materialise(payload_i)  (zero egress)
    end

    Note over A,DB: Stage 2 — divergent call forwarded live and captured
    A->>F: generate_response(request_N)  (unmatched messages)
    F->>S: active_session()
    F->>Sig: extract_signature(model=…, messages=…)
    F->>Cursor: respond_or_forward(signature_N)
    Note right of Cursor: messages_hash differs from span[N].messages_hash
    Cursor-->>F: None  (no recorded span matches)
    F->>C: assert_not_frozen(session)
    Note right of C: BRANCH mode permits divergence — no raise
    F->>W: wrapped.generate_response(request_N)
    W-->>F: live result (real HTTP / SDK call)
    F->>C: build_live_span(session, model_name=…, messages=…, content=…)
    C-->>F: new Span(kind=LLM, messages_hash=…, raw_attributes.gen_ai.response=…)
    F->>Cursor: record_new(span)
    Cursor->>DB: INSERT spans row (new span_id, parent = current branch)
    Cursor->>Cursor: advance cursor
    F-->>A: live result
    Note over A,DB: New span now lives on the BRANCH trace and can be<br/>replayed as deterministic cache on subsequent FROZEN runs.
